  values ($mw$skf-drive-up-card$mw$, $mw$SKF Drive-Up Reference Card: Clearance Reduction and Axial Drive-Up for Tapered-Bore Bearings (24 to 1 800 mm)$mw$, $mw$The complete SKF pocket card: reduction of radial internal clearance, axial drive-up distance for 1:12 and 1:30 tapers, and lock-nut tightening angle, for spherical roller and CARB bearings from 24 mm to 1 800 mm bore.$mw$, $mw$Spherical roller bearings and CARB toroidal roller bearings with a tapered bore are **always** mounted with an interference fit. SKF lists three ways to get the right interference:

1. Measure the **clearance reduction** with feeler gauges (preferred; see the [full procedure](/article/taper-bore-bearing-adapter-sleeve-skf)).
2. Measure the **lock-nut tightening angle** from the line-to-line position (small bores only).
3. Measure the **axial drive-up distance s** from the line-to-line position (dial indicator or hydraulic-nut gauge).

All dimensions in **mm**, angle in degrees.

| Bore d over | Bore d incl. | Reduction min | Reduction max | s (1:12) min | s (1:12) max | s (1:30) min | s (1:30) max | Nut angle α (1:12) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 24 | 30 | 0.010 | 0.015 | 0.25 | 0.29 | - | - | 100° |
| 30 | 40 | 0.015 | 0.020 | 0.30 | 0.35 | - | - | 115° |
| 40 | 50 | 0.020 | 0.025 | 0.37 | 0.44 | - | - | 130° |
| 50 | 65 | 0.025 | 0.035 | 0.45 | 0.54 | 1.15 | 1.35 | 115° |
| 65 | 80 | 0.035 | 0.040 | 0.55 | 0.65 | 1.40 | 1.65 | 130° |
| 80 | 100 | 0.040 | 0.050 | 0.66 | 0.79 | 1.65 | 2.00 | 150° |
| 100 | 120 | 0.050 | 0.060 | 0.79 | 0.95 | 2.00 | 2.35 | |
| 120 | 140 | 0.060 | 0.075 | 0.93 | 1.10 | 2.30 | 2.80 | |
| 140 | 160 | 0.070 | 0.085 | 1.05 | 1.30 | 2.65 | 3.20 | |
| 160 | 180 | 0.080 | 0.095 | 1.20 | 1.45 | 3.00 | 3.60 | |
| 180 | 200 | 0.090 | 0.105 | 1.30 | 1.60 | 3.30 | 4.00 | |
